{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers","id":280052,"title":"2e Brainstorm: Kuruth Triggers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-13T13:38:32-07:00","id":280052,"title":"2e Brainstorm: Kuruth Triggers","content":"Sorry for the silence on the 2nd Edition front, lots of things all happened at once.<br /> <br /> Anyway. I'm getting the book ready for editing and one thing's staring at me. Kuruth triggers.<br /> <br /> Long story short, each werewolf has a thing that triggers death rage. If she's at the end of the Harmony scale, this could be something like &quot;my auspice moon is in the sky&quot;. If she's not quite at the extremes, it might be &quot;I saw my auspice moon in the sky&quot;. If she's close to balance, it might be &quot;spending a scene in the light of my auspice moon&quot;. And I'm trying to come up with plenty of examples, in three categories.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Passive</b> triggers are the &quot;auspice moon in the sky&quot;. They're events or circumstances that just happen. The werewolf can't avoid them, <i>something</i> happens and boom, <i>Kuruth.</i><br /> \u2022 <b>Common</b> triggers are the &quot;seeing auspice moon&quot;. They're common, but they need the werewolf to interact with them. You need to see the moon, or taste blood, or whatevs.<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific</b> triggers are the &quot;scene in the moonlight&quot;. They're not common, but a werewolf may be pushed to encounter one.<br /> <br /> I've got a couple of examples of each, but could do with more. So I'm throwing it open to the forums. Help me out and suggest things!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T13:45:28-07:00","id":280069,"title":"","content":"Quick query for clarification for the readers, Stew - Kuruth triggers cause a roll to resist Death Rage rather than automatically shoving you into Death Rage, if I remember correctly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T13:51:50-07:00","id":280099,"title":"","content":"Triggers send you into <i>Wasu-Im</i>, the first stage of Death Rage. You can pull yourself out of that, but it does make you go a bit weird while you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T13:53:34-07:00","id":280102,"title":"","content":"I will try to think of some...<br /> About seeing the auspice moon, how it would work for the Irraka?<br /> And what about silver triggering Death Rage?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T13:55:00-07:00","id":280103,"title":"","content":"Ummmm, wow...I will think on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:01:39-07:00","id":280113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280102#post280102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will try to think of some...<br /> About seeing the auspice moon, how it would work for the Irraka?<br /> And what about silver triggering Death Rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>The new moon is still a moon. The only time it doesn't give light is during an actual eclipse.<br /> <br /> Some things, like taking damage from silver, are triggers for every werewolf regardless of Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:03:57-07:00","id":280117,"title":"","content":"Y'know what? Here's the current triggers section:<br /> <br /> <b>Passive Triggers</b><br /> Your auspice moon is in the sky<br /> Smelling blood<br /> <br /> <b>Common Triggers</b><br /> Seeing your auspice moon<br /> Swallowing human blood<br /> <br /> <b>Specific Triggers</b><br /> Spending a scene in the light of your Auspice moon<br /> Swallowing your own blood<br /> <br /> <b>General Triggers</b><br /> Spending too long in Gauru<br /> Taking Gauru outside of combat<br /> Taking damage from silver<br /> Forced into <i>Kuruth</i> by an Elodoth<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:06:22-07:00","id":280118,"title":"","content":"\u2022 <b>Passive</b> A non pack Werewolf enters your territory without permission.<br /> \u2022 <b>Common</b> You see a non-pack Werewolf in your territory.<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific</b> A non-pack Werewolf challanges your pack's authority within the territory.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Passive</b> A Spirit crosses the gauntlet in your territory.<br /> \u2022 <b>Common</b> You hear animals react to the Spirit.<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific</b> You hear and understand the animals specifically warning about a Spirit.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Passive</b> Auspice moon in the sky.<br /> \u2022 <b>Common</b> You hear wolves howl at your Auspice moon.<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific</b> You hear wolves howl at your Auspice moon while moonlight touches your flesh.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Passive</b> A wolf dies nearby.<br /> \u2022 <b>Common</b> You meet a human who's recently killed a wolf (you must be able to smell the blood and see his face).<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific</b> You see a human kill a wolf for sport.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Passive</b> A human shaman performs a ritual nearby<br /> \u2022 <b>Common</b> You meet a human who practices a Spirit based religion.<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific</b> And you know about it (see an religious necklace, they talk about it).<br /> <br /> I've long felt since Werewolves want to keep the spirit and Flesh apart; humans who wish to harmoniosuly merge Material and Spiritual would make brilliant antagonists / foils.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can't think of a themed set for this one. I know it's more Changeling than Werewolf, but here it is anyway.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Specific</b>: Seeing a young girl lost in the forest. (&quot;young&quot; can mean &quot;pre puberty&quot;, &quot;pre menstruation&quot; or &quot;virgin&quot; - depending on which metaphor Werewolf is using)<br /> <br /> Another one without a set.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Specific</b>: Seeing a lost sheep. (I'm riffing on the idea that savagely eaten cattle is sometimes portrayed as the first warning sign of a nearby Werewolf; and sheep are stereotypical wolf victims).<br /> <br /> <br /> Before I continue, are these useful DigitalRaven?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-13-2014, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:21:41-07:00","id":280130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280117#post280117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know what? Here's the current triggers section:<br /> <br /> <b>Passive Triggers</b><br /> Your auspice moon is in the sky<br /> Smelling blood<br /> <br /> <b>Common Triggers</b><br /> Seeing your auspice moon<br /> <b>Swallowing human blood</b><br /> <br /> <b>Specific Triggers</b><br /> Spending a scene in the light of your Auspice moon<br /> <b>Swallowing your own blood</b><br /> <br /> <b>General Triggers</b><br /> Spending too long in Gauru<br /> Taking Gauru outside of combat<br /> Taking damage from silver<br /> Forced into <i>Kuruth</i> by an Elodoth</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolded, the specific trigger is easier than the common one. As anyone whose been in a fist fight can attest it's pretty easy to end up swallowing some of your own blood, especially if you receive a solid smack to the face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:27:50-07:00","id":280155,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's the case for werewolves. It's basically &quot;take a targeted shot to the face&quot; vs. &quot;deal damage with a bite attack&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:28:48-07:00","id":280156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280118#post280118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before I continue, are these useful DigitalRaven?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are the kind of thing I'm looking for, yes. Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:35:17-07:00","id":280162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280155#post280155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's the case for werewolves. It's basically &quot;take a targeted shot to the face&quot; vs. &quot;deal damage with a bite attack&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. The Common trigger can be deliberately avoided, and only occurs when hunting a specific breed of prey. The Specific trigger can occur in any fight, or as a result of a botched athletics roll. Basically I can think of whole arcs I've run where the first would never have been an issue, while I can think of few chapters where the second wouldn't have been a possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:44:09-07:00","id":280165,"title":"","content":"A few more then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Common</b>: Get attacked in a dishonourable fashion.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Common</b>: Smell non-pack Werewolf urine in your territory.<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific: </b>They've pissed on the spot where you've marked your territory.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Specific: </b>You encounter a moon rock.<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific: </b>Someone who brought land on the moon mentions it to you.<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific: </b>You talk to a neo-pagan about her worship of the Moon - practices that Mother Luna would find offensive if she cared enough to notice.<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific: </b>You witness a Mage using a Moon related Yantra that contradicts Mother Luna's history/personality/known attributes.<br /> \u2022 <b>Specific: </b>You encounter a legitimate worshipper of/an actual Luna deity unrelated to Mother Luna.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T14:58:04-07:00","id":280173,"title":"","content":"Now for genuine input!<br /> <br /> <b>Affection</b><br /> \u2022 Passive: Hear about someone you love or respect being injured or insulted.<br /> \u2022 Common: Seeing someone you love or respect being injured or insulted.<br /> \u2022 Specific: Seeing someone you love or respect being injured.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspiration</b><br /> \u2022 Passive: An event happens to runs counter to one of your Aspirations.<br /> \u2022 Common: Someone verbally opposes the pursuit of one of your Aspirations.<br /> \u2022 Specific: Someone physically opposes the pursuit of one of your Aspirations.<br /> <br /> <b>Condition</b><br /> \u2022 Passive: You are subject to a negative Condition<br /> \u2022 Common: You are subject to a Persistent Negative Condition<br /> \u2022 Specific: You gain a Beat from a Persistent Negative Condition<br /> <br /> <b>Hunt</b><br /> \u2022Passive: An obstacle stands in the way of your hunt<br /> \u2022 Common: You fail to capture your prey during a hunt<br /> \u2022 Specific: Your efforts are not helpful in capturing the prey during a hunt, even if your pack does succeed<br /> <br /> <b>Social</b><br /> \u2022 Passive: You fail to Open any Doors (in Social Maneuvering)<br /> \u2022 Common: You're Alternatives are refused (in Social Maneuvering)<br /> \u2022 Specific: You attempt to Force Doors and fail (in Social Maneuvering)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T15:09:03-07:00","id":280183,"title":"","content":"With the emphasis on sacred prey I could see something cool based off of that, but actually thinking about it, encountering new humans and spirits and werewolves bringing you close to rage would be an unnecessary burden. So what about contact with a (new) supernatural they can't identify (maybe just in their own territory)? Being threatened in their own territory? Seeing non-Uratha packmates killed? Being immobilized or confined? The presence of a rage-influenced Wound? I'm not exactly sure how Wounds work. Being forced to do something they don't want to do by a non-Uratha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-13-2014, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T15:42:25-07:00","id":280203,"title":"","content":"Gonna focus on harmony specific ones;<br /> <br /> <b>Specific-Too human;</b><br /> \u2022 Full moon on the sky<br /> \u2022 Scent of raw meat or sight of a carcass (human or animal)<br /> \u2022 Someone challenging authority<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T19:06:59-07:00","id":280406,"title":"","content":"<b>Prey</b><br /> Passive: Seeing your tribes' prey<br /> Common: Seeing your tribes' prey try to run away from/attack a werewolf<br /> Specific: Seeing your tribes' prey escape from/kill a werewolf<br /> <br /> You could also expand on the Silver thing a little bit:<br /> <br /> Passive: Seeing silver.<br /> Common: Touching silver.<br /> Specific: Taking damage from silver.<br /> <br /> If my understanding is right, being injured by silver would still be a thing for everyone, but this way silver would have more of a psychological impact on characters who are less stable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T02:15:21-07:00","id":280755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280155#post280155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's the case for werewolves. It's basically &quot;take a targeted shot to the face&quot; vs. &quot;deal damage with a bite attack&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't quite specific in the description. Ergo, you'd have several, several people asking about it if published as this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T02:27:49-07:00","id":280756,"title":"","content":"Passive: The night falls.<br /> Common: Scent a woman's period.<br /> Specific: Witness a senior tribemate (higher Honorary rank) break your tribal oath.<br /> <br /> Common: Being cut off in traffic.<br /> Common: Seeing someone morbidly overweight.<br /> Specific: Having your personal space violated repeatedly (picture public transportation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 10-14-2014, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T02:37:26-07:00","id":280758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280756#post280756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Common: Being cut off in traffic.<br /> Common: Seeing someone morbidly overweight.<br /> Specific: Having your personal space violated repeatedly (picture public transportation).</div> </div> </div> </div>I spose they are jokes, right? Becuase as rather overweight person I feel very ofended if that would be Kuruth Trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-14-2014, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T02:41:14-07:00","id":280760,"title":"","content":"As I understand, those are Triggers for Kuruth that lend from Harmony score, as <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/one-foot-in-flesh-and-one-in-spirit/\" target=\"_blank\">stated in spoiler</a>. As this, I understand that Specific Triggers are for balanced characters ( probably Harmony 4-6 ), Common are for slightly unhinged ( Harmony 7-8 and 2-3 ) and Passive are for extremes ( Harmony 9-10 and 1-2)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:25:34-07:00","id":280896,"title":"","content":"Passive: Looking at a Wound<br /> Common: Being under the area of influence of a Wound or interacting with a wounded spirit<br /> Specific: Being attacked by a wounded spirit.<br /> <br /> Passive: Seeing someone breaking your tribal ban<br /> Common: Seeing a werewolf of higher ranking than you breaking the ban<br /> Specific: Breaking your tribal ban","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 10-14-2014, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:36:39-07:00","id":280900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280162#post280162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno. The Common trigger can be deliberately avoided, and only occurs when hunting a specific breed of prey. The Specific trigger can occur in any fight, or as a result of a botched athletics roll. Basically I can think of whole arcs I've run where the first would never have been an issue, while I can think of few chapters where the second wouldn't have been a possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. I'll think on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:49:15-07:00","id":280909,"title":"","content":"Also, thank you all. I've got enough Kuruth triggers for the book now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:58:33-07:00","id":280919,"title":"","content":"So maybe next supplement for the gameline will be &quot;Great Book of Triggers&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-14-2014, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T06:02:09-07:00","id":280921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280909#post280909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, thank you all. I've got enough Kuruth triggers for the book now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I still have some more!<br /> <br /> Passive: Packmate or loved one being insulted<br /> Common: Packmate or loved one being injured<br /> Specific: Packmate or loved one suffering a lethal or aggravated wound<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T07:18:21-07:00","id":280981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Common: Seeing someone morbidly overweight. </div> </div> </div>This one I actually like, and it's not so offensive...the key word here is <b>Morbidly </b>overweight like 500 pounds plus, unable to move or take care of yourself. Werewolves are the epitome of physicality, able to run for extraordinary amounts of time and distance. So I could really actually see a werewolf of sufficient harmony looking at someone in that condition and feeling disgust and anger at them for putting others in the position of taking care of them instead of doing it themselves. I can totally picture it. But I won't go further...don't wanna draw this thread off topic too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T07:54:00-07:00","id":281006,"title":"","content":"My first though was easy, plentiful prey. Can't run that fast or for so long and can provide plenty of food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T07:54:54-07:00","id":281007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Scorpion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280981#post280981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I could really actually see a werewolf of sufficient harmony looking at someone in that condition and feeling disgust and anger at them for putting others in the position of taking care of them instead of doing it themselves...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or seeing them as a delicious, mobile, easily-dispatched sack of protein, calcium, and most importantly, calories; all the things that a growing, active Uratha needs.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:00:53-07:00","id":281010,"title":"","content":"So why not throw in disabled people, too? Wheelchairs, life support systems. Hospitals would just send them into a feeding frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:04:32-07:00","id":281014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Scorpion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280981#post280981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one I actually like, and it's not so offensive...the key word here is <b>Morbidly </b>overweight like 500 pounds plus, unable to move or take care of yourself. Werewolves are the epitome of physicality, able to run for extraordinary amounts of time and distance. So I could really actually see a werewolf of sufficient harmony looking at someone in that condition and feeling disgust and anger at them for putting others in the position of taking care of them instead of doing it themselves. I can totally picture it. But I won't go further...don't wanna draw this thread off topic too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see this as xenophobic tendencies in some Uratha philosphies, but no in the kind of &quot;you see someone overweight and goes in to Death Rage&quot;. Also, analogy would be when Awakened see someone who was dull and must cast vulgar spell then, to show how awesome magic is. <b>It's stupid</b>. ( Not counting disrespectful to people like me... )<br /> <br /> More sense would be that Uratha goes in to <i>Wasu-Im</i> when his feelings are hurt, like women not wanting his advances. Not that they see someone overweight...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=281010#post281010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why not throw in disabled people, too? Wheelchairs, life support systems. Hospitals would just send them into a feeding frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-14-2014, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:22:35-07:00","id":281029,"title":"","content":"I know it's a tad too late, but here are my 2 cents:<br /> <br /> <b>Specific:</b> Someone's being all dominant, or assumes a dominant posture, whilst addressing you; e.g. staring you in the eyes, getting all up in your face, showing lots of teeth when he talks, raising and/or deepening his voice whilst speaking to deliberately talk you down, walking slow circles around you, or standing with shoulders squared, chest out, and feet planted whilst you are sitting down.<br /> <b>Specific:</b> Someone's bleeding all over your territory, be it on the trees in your park, the grass on your lawn, or the floor of your bedroom.<br /> <br /> <b>Common:</b> Lingering too long in the presence of juvenile prey items; puppies, kittens, bunnies, even small children. To the Herd, they may seem cute, adorable even. To the Wolf, however...<br /> <b>Common:</b> Lingering too long in the presence of enemies, whether or not these are actual or just designated enemies. Lunge, fight, bite, tear; the Wolf demands it.<br /> <br /> <b>Passive:</b> Seeing rapid side-to-side movement or watching prey run away from you; hearing their panicked cries and whimpers; catching the scent of terror-induced incontinence; what predator does not delight in the thrill of the chase, in being feared by the hunted?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:38:09-07:00","id":281040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=281010#post281010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why not throw in disabled people, too? Wheelchairs, life support systems. Hospitals would just send them into a feeding frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not indeed? The specifics are, of course, up to the developers, but personally, I see Kuruth as more than a state of &quot;THIS MAKES ME FUCKING MAD, RAAAWR!&quot; It's also the Monster Within pushing out, that unfathomably ancient beast of incarnate savagery whose biological and spiritual imperatives revolve around hunting, killing, and eating. It is also the almighty, god-slaying apex predator who will brook no bullshit from anything, whether lesser beings (prey) or fellow predators, unless that adversary prove itself to be superior (and this superiority, or lack thereof, *will* be tested). Being taken over or surrending to Kuruth, at least for me, is that nature, the Monster Within, tearing the Human You apart; one meaning that can be ascribed to the &quot;death&quot; in Death Rage.<br /> <br /> (Of course, if any of the devs around would want to correct me on this, they would be more than welcome to. This is, after all, just the interpretation for Kuruth that I tend to use in my games, aside from how it is defined in the books; I would want to rectify this if I am in error.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3702,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","user":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","date":". 10-14-2014, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T08:58:05-07:00","id":281102,"title":"","content":"It seems more about calling to your true nature.<br /> <br /> The uratha aren't, outside of the Pure, angry at the moon, but seeing the moon can trigger it. As can the scent of blood, which wouldn't just make you angry, but would tap into the hunter inside of you. Considering Uratha have a well known incident in the past that revolved around taking down their weakening alpha, I don't see why, if morbidly obese people acted as a trigger, the disabled wouldn't fit either.<br /> <br /> Emotional trauma seems to do it as well, more likely as an instinctive 'retreat' to your bestial side as a way to avoid dealing with the human pain of the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:23:07-07:00","id":281133,"title":"","content":"I actually agree with you on the bit about the disabled, nofather; additionally, I would fold &quot;severely wounded&quot; into that category as well. Though, it is less that Uratha hate the disabled, and more about their savage instincts regarding weak and infirm prey. The bit about the First Pack killing Urafarah was not particularly because they hated weakness; it was because, as their alpha, Urfarah's weakness also became the First Pack's weakness. It was making them far less effective at maintaining the balance of Flesh and Spirit, and it would inevitably lead to their destruction, if not stopped. Killing him was not an act of hate, but a necessary evil (But of course, the legend in your games might vary).<br /> <br /> In any case, I'd think a werewolf would only start regarding others of his own race as prey items as his Harmony drops and he becomes less human and more like a wolf/predator spirit. So, at least in my opinion, &quot;Lingering in the presence of young/vulnerable/disabled prey&quot; would be a Common trigger, a thing for Uratha of lower Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:38:04-07:00","id":281149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=280758#post280758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I spose they are jokes, right? Becuase as rather overweight person I feel very ofended if that would be Kuruth Trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't. Why would you be offended by that? Obese human = slower, easier to catch prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:43:13-07:00","id":281156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=281133#post281133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, I'd think a werewolf would only start regarding others of his own race as prey items as his Harmony drops and he becomes less human and more like a wolf/predator spirit. So, at least in my opinion, &quot;Lingering in the presence of young/vulnerable/disabled prey&quot; would be a Common trigger, a thing for Uratha of lower Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>You understand that Common threats are somehow for middle advanced Harmony levels, right? Like Harmony 7-8 or 2-3.<br /> <br /> It was said that both Harmony extremes ( <b>both</b> Harmony 10 and Harmony 0 ) are suitable to those outside Triggers, they just react in diffrent way - Harmony 10 character is <b>too much</b> human, and wipes his action under Death Rage. He is typical &quot;cursed Joe&quot; of horror movies. Harmony 1 Uratha is <b>too much</b> wolf spirit, and he almost never assume human form, disregarding Herd more as food than persons. And they are <b>both</b> under Passive Triggers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;[FONT=Cambria</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Foot in Flesh and One in Spirit&quot;[/FONT]] That perfect position of balance comes at Harmony 5. When your Harmony is higher, you\u2019re closer to the flesh than the spirit. At Harmony 10, you can\u2019t enter the Shadow and you need to burn Essence to shapeshift at all (except when you enter Kuruth). At Harmony 0, you\u2019re trapped in the Shadow. You need to spend Essence and roll to not shapeshift when you face an emotional stimulus \u2014 and you\u2019re laden with spirit bans over and above those from totem and lodge. Balanced Harmony makes shapeshifting easier, making it a reflexive action or even removing the roll entirely. It also means that Kuruth triggers become more specific \u2014 you go from your auspice moon rising, to seeing your auspice moon, to seeing your own reflection in the light of your auspice moon. When you face Kuruth, you can hold it off for longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read this spoiler section in full.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=281149#post281149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't. Why would you be offended by that? Obese human = slower, easier to catch prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this should be reson to change in to 2.5 meter monster? EVERY TIME you see someone obese?!<br /> <br /> About &quot;fit Tiggers over disabled&quot; - if Onyx Path would used this as Triggers for players characters it would lead to one big lawsuit. And I would be one of their lawsuit supporters. Basically you are saying &quot;being ill or disabled should be bad for <b>Werewolf</b> players&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-14-2014, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:00:32-07:00","id":281188,"title":"","content":"I am well aware of the Kuruth Triggers being discussed being applicable to both extremes of the Harmony spectrum, wyrdhamster, thank you very much. I have also read through the blog spoilers, and I am, in fact, running a 2e game right now with a view to converting fully to Werewolf after the book comes out, so I re-read through it every so often, if only for the inspiration.<br /> <br /> I am also somehow getting the impression that you are taking this discussion a little too personally. Please don't; not only is it unhelpful with regard to intellectual discourse, but we are also not attacking you personally, as a matter of fact. We are not bashing on overweight or disabled people here, we are not saying they shouldn't play the game. What we are saying, if, indeed, we are saying anything at all, is that <b>within the context of the goddamned game,</b> a werewolf sufficiently unbalanced would start looking at humans as prey, and the more easily caught and eaten, the better. Because that is how real life predators operate towards their prey.<br /> <br /> And remember: these triggers only cause Wasu-Im; they don't make you into a 2.5m-tall monster on their own, they just initiate the process. A process which, mind you, can be delayed, if not halted completely. Of course, that's only how I understood it the last time I read Stew's blog post about Kuruth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3702,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","user":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","date":". 10-14-2014, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T11:44:18-07:00","id":281309,"title":"","content":"I forget if the blog mentioned it but I'm hoping we get some space for personalized triggers for werewolves who have been through some stuff. I could see Azlu triggering an arachnophobe and so forth.<br /> <br /> It also seems like something you could add to Lodges to further differentiate the Uratha members from their kin.<br /> <br /> It's too moral for core werewolves, but considering werewolves are part spirit, I could see some getting twitchy when (if they're optimistic about humankind) someone nearby gives into their vice, or (if they're pessimistic) their virtue. Essentially triggering a 'this should not be' sense, as the people are going against what the werewolf sees as their true nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-14-2014, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T11:50:17-07:00","id":281334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=281309#post281309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget if the blog mentioned it but I'm hoping we get some space for personalized triggers for werewolves who have been through some stuff. I could see Azlu triggering an arachnophobe and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have actually been wanting to ask if we are going to be able to customize Kuruth triggers (other than General ones, of course) for our characters, with the frequency (from Specific to Passive) depending on how far along they are on either half of the Harmony spectrum. Because that would be insanely awesome and make a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T01:51:36-07:00","id":282058,"title":"","content":"The obesity/disability tangent <b>ends here</b>. As does saying &quot;you shouldn't be upset because intellectual discourse.&quot; Trying to score points off other posters with smug pseudointellectualism is not conductive to actually discussing things.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is a game where our protagonists already stand a very good chance of murdering their loved ones and only noticing when they return to lucidity covered in blood and entrails. Precisely what sets that off is a bunch of factors, of which we have examples in the book that this thread has been very helpful in producing. Those factors relate to the state of <i>being a werewolf</i>, not to the process of hunting or to real-world predation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T02:04:57-07:00","id":282064,"title":"","content":"Glad we return to the sanity by the developer. As to the question about Triggers - can we know what kind of categories <b>will</b> go to the corebook? What from the brainstorm pass? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T04:34:03-07:00","id":282159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DigitalRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/280052-2e-brainstorm-kuruth-triggers?p=282058#post282058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obesity/disability tangent <b>ends here</b>. As does saying &quot;you shouldn't be upset because intellectual discourse.&quot; Trying to score points off other posters with smug pseudointellectualism is not conductive to actually discussing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I'm all for the discussion continuing in a productive direction, in any case. *thumbs up*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf is a game where our protagonists already stand a very good chance of murdering their loved ones and only noticing when they return to lucidity covered in blood and entrails. Precisely what sets that off is a bunch of factors, of which we have examples in the book that this thread has been very helpful in producing. Those factors relate to the state of <i>being a werewolf</i>, not to the process of hunting or to real-world predation. </div> </div> </div>It has been a long time since I've played/ran 1e, but the problems I encountered with regard to Death Rage are that: 1.) Some of the triggers, namely betrayal and loved ones being endangered, were quite vague; 2.) Kuruth was so binary; you either failed the roll and went apeshit, or you maintained control. Combined with #1, invoking Kuruth thus meant the risk of derailing scenes or even storylines, unless the Storyteller planned around it very carefully; 3.) Kuruth, with the way it was, established Uratha as irrational, Rage-filled beasts, and while I don't argue much against this, I always thought it could have been more interesting. I mean, I recall parts of the fluff suggesting that Auspices influence how Uratha feel and express their Rage. If I may make a suggestion, how neat would it be if, for example, an Irraka in the throes of Death Rage becomes an implacable hunter, relentlessly pursuing an enemy while retaining the capability to use Cunning to its advantage? An Elodoth becomes judgment incarnate, prioritizing those who offend the laws it holds most dear to dispense bloody retribution upon? Cahaliths become like the Maenads of Greek myth, glorious and exultant in their savagery, making it all the more horrifying when a normally reasonable Cahalith comes to terms with what she's done whilst fallen to Kuruth? Etc.<br /> <br /> It is my opinion that 2e has only improved upon Kuruth. Splitting it between Wasu-Im and Basu-Im took away the binariness, and Harmony playing a role in how easily an Uratha falls into it only contributes nuance to how it can be imagined and thus roleplayed. I hope that 2e continues down this direction. *thumbs up*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3702,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","user":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","date":". 10-15-2014, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}